#==============================================================================================
#
#   ljs - Run JavaScript files with luce-js, like QuickJS's qjs
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of qjs.c (QuickJS 2026-06-04): `ljs [options] [file [args]]` runs a script or
#       a module, `-e EXPR` evaluates an expression, and without a file (or with -i) ljs
#       runs QuickJS's REPL, repl.js, whose bytecode tests/repl.lucb holds as qjs links
#       repl.c (both are generated by the compiler: `cd tests && ../build/ljsc -s -c -o
#       repl.lucb -m repl.js`, as the Makefile runs qjsc; tests/tools.py checks that it is
#       current). Every option of qjs is ported, with the same short and long spellings,
#       combined short options (-qd) and exit statuses: -h, -e, -i, -m, --script, --strict,
#       -I, --std, -T (trace the allocations), -d (dump the memory usage, and with -q the
#       instantiation times: `ljs -qd` is `make stats`), --memory-limit, --stack-size,
#       --no-unhandled-rejection, -s, --strip-source and -q.
#
#       Shared-library modules are the native modules ljs links in and registers: "bjson"
#       (tests/bjson.c) and the examples "fib" and "point", imported as "./bjson.so" or
#       "bjson" and so on.
#
#       Differences from the C: the program is named ljs in its messages; the default stack
#       size is luce-js's (js_default_stack_size).
#
#       Build: luce-base build tests/ljs.lucb -o build/ljs
#
#       QuickJS stand alone interpreter
#
#       Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Fabrice Bellard
#       Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Charlie Gordon
#
#       Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this
#       software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal in the Software
#       without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify,
#       merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to
#       permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following
#       conditions: the above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included
#       in all copies or substantial portions of the Software. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS
#       IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.
#
